  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Calling Out Your Name (Rich Mullins cover)** (1 other source): Notes list banter and Good Bones by Maggie Smith alongside this track, apparently as separate track material [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Armies of the Lord**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Need More Bandages**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n- **Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Dawn of Revelation**: rare: 12 archived performances [2]\n- **Hello Sarah**: rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Calling Out Your Name (Rich Mullins cover)**: back after 42 archived shows (816 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Pictue of My Dress**: back after 97 archived shows (1268 days); rare: 10 archived performances [2]\n- **Genesis 3 23**: back after 78 archived shows (1057 days); rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2026-05-26** (recommended): soundboard; 24 songs; 116 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children, banter and genesis, solo transition and [1]\n- Taper enjoyed waiting indoors with friends before the show [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2026-05-26**: taped by Kyle Kennelly & Emerald Green; transferred by Kyle Kennelly; source: SBD [Engineer: Brandon Eggleston] > PCM-A10 + Tascam FR-AV2 > DPA4060s (Healy On Stage) [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Dan Denney: [The Mountain Goats at Brooklyn Bowl Nashville](https://www.dandenney.com/no-reserv-ai-tions/the-mountain-goats/) [3]",
